law.text:
		The Commission shall have the following powers and duties:

Study and evaluate issues related to women's health, including maternal health, mental health, access to reproductive care, chronic conditions, and health outcomes;


Examine the intersection of social determinants of health and their impact on women's health outcomes;


Conduct public hearings, facilitate stakeholder engagement, and consult with subject-matter experts as necessary;


Identify systemic barriers to equitable health care access for women and recommend policies to address such barriers; and


Develop and make recommendations to the General Assembly for legislative, regulatory, and budgetary changes or policies to improve women's health outcomes in the Commonwealth.
